path: /artifact/typescript-7-with-the-native-go-compiler
created_at: 2026-09-08T14:55:08.289479+00:00
needs_review: true
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> CONTRADICTS [node:b6cc5895-5e52-462a-aab2-c934ba921825] @ 2026-09-08T14:55:08.289479+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T14:55:08.289479+00:00

TypeScript 7 with the native Go compiler is generally available - 7.0.2 on npm - so the stack's assumption holds and scaffolding does not need a fallback to the 5.x line. The plan was written when a June 2026 release candidate was still the expectation; the verification it asked for has now been done. Vite 8, Svelte 5, Astro 7 and Fastify 5 are likewise all real releases, so nothing in the assumed stack is aspirational.
---
[event:665e5b05-3470-4a93-9117-5d5dcc0283f3]
