contradicted at capture of 8e7f3005-1043-45a9-994b-366f80431b08
---
[event:1d1bccdc-7247-4f76-85aa-e98aa6ac5f60]
node_id: e43574bd-bdb9-493c-83fb-7f89fb4f9d8f
type: contradiction_raised
weight: 1.0
polarity: -1
source: agent-surface
created_at: 2026-09-08T15:04:16.472674+00:00

half of this is wrong and it was captured today: TypeScript 7 is indeed GA, but 'scaffolding does not need a fallback' is false - typescript-eslint 8 hard-refuses to load against 7 and svelte-check peers ^5||^6, so the scaffold pins 6.0.3
---
[node:8e7f3005-1043-45a9-994b-366f80431b08]
type: decision
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/typescript-is-pinned-to-the-6-x-line-no
created_at: 2026-09-08T15:04:16.351954+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-08T15:04:16.351954+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T15:04:16.351954+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:e43574bd-bdb9-493c-83fb-7f89fb4f9d8f] @ 2026-09-08T15:04:16.351954+00:00

TypeScript is pinned to the 6.x line, not 7, even though 7 is generally available. The compiler shipped ahead of its ecosystem: typescript-eslint 8 declares a peer range of >=4.8.4 <6.1.0 and refuses to load against 7 at import time rather than merely warning, and svelte-check peers ^5 || ^6. TypeScript 6.0.3 is the highest version the whole toolchain accepts, so it is the pin. Reaching for --legacy-peer-deps instead would have produced a lint setup that imports a parser its own dependency rejects. Move to 7 when typescript-eslint and svelte-check widen their ranges, not before.
---
