-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.673656+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f29aa338-eddb-456b-97ad-00b602cb9a42] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.673656+00:00

Secret scrubbing runs in two layers and neither is redundant. Exact-value scrubbing rewrites any string containing a credential this process actually holds, which is the reliable half but only covers what was registered at boot; pattern scrubbing catches credential shapes nobody registered - a bearer token from a dependency, a database URL carrying a password, a JWT - which is the half that covers what was forgotten. A registered key matches no pattern and a third-party credential appears in no registry, so dropping either layer opens a real hole. Values shorter than eight characters are ignored on purpose: a three-character secret matches inside ordinary words and turns the whole report into redaction noise.
---
