-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:35.029534+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:35.029534+00:00

The runtime floor is Node 24, not 22. TypeScript type stripping is stable there and needs no flag, which removes a whole class of failure: on 22 every script carries an experimental strip-types flag, that flag interacts badly with the test runner's argument ordering, and the resulting breakage reports a missing module rather than a missing flag. CI and the LAN machine both run 24, so the floor matches reality instead of aspiring below it.
